        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1300",
        ":question/problem": "If $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨-3,1⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨4,6⟩$, then $\\overset{\\to }{u}+\\overset{\\to }{v}=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{u}+\\overset{\\to }{v} & =⟨-3,1⟩+⟨4,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3+4,1+6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"
